```
id: SPL-025
name: WAF block spike
description: A high number of blocked requests against a web application within a short interval.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Initial Access
mitre_technique: T1190 Exploit Public-Facing Application
severity: Medium
data_source: index=waf
false_positives: Authorized scans; releases that trigger legitimate rule matches.
tuning: Exclude scanner addresses; baseline per application.
test_method: Send a burst of requests with common attack strings to a lab application.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=waf action IN ("blocked","block") earliest=-1h
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count AS blocks dc(src) AS distinct_clients values(signature) AS rules BY _time, dest
| where blocks>=50
| sort - blocks
